    <briefdescription>
<para>Replicated Growable Array (RGA). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A sequence CRDT that preserves insertion order. Each element is tagged with a unique <ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1crdt_1_1_dot" kindref="compound">Dot</ref>. Insertions specify a predecessor <ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1crdt_1_1_dot" kindref="compound">Dot</ref> (the element after which to insert); deletions tombstone the element&apos;s <ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1crdt_1_1_dot" kindref="compound">Dot</ref>.</para>
<para>This implementation uses a vector for O(n) insert/delete, which is acceptable for sequences of up to ~10 k elements.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Element type. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
